From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:44:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Use the DSU operating
 points

Include the DSU operating points on the Cubie A7S and give the DSU its
supply, DCDC5, the regulator of the Cortex-A55 cluster.

No document names the DSU supply: the datasheet and the schematic of
the board carry no DSU net. The silicon does: at fixed CPU rates, the
highest DSU rate that runs moves with DCDC5 and not with DCDC3, the
regulator of the Cortex-A76 cluster. The DSU driver finds the A55
policy by this supply, as cpu-supply of cpu0.

A kernel without the DSU driver leaves the node unused, and the DSU
stays at the rate the boot firmware set. With the driver but without
cpufreq, the driver waits for the CPU policies and changes nothing.

Not covered: the DSU on boards whose DSU supply is not that of the A55
cluster; the driver needs the two to be one regulator.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the DSU takes DCDC5,
the supply of the A55 cluster, a forced DSU minimum raises DCDC5 and
leaves DCDC3 alone, and the DSU rate follows the A55 policy.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index e76f308e21ba..e50a089056e7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 
 #include "sun60i-a733.dtsi"
 #include "sun60i-a733-cpu-opp.dtsi"
+#include "sun60i-a733-dsu-opp.dtsi"
 
 #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/leds/common.h>
@@ -125,6 +126,10 @@ &cpu7 {
 	operating-points-v2 = <&cluster1_opp>;
 };
 
+&dsu {
+	dsu-supply = <&reg_dcdc5>;
+};
+
 &ehci1 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
